{"id":"resp_b61812532425f2ba","created_at":1795544531,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_a3c0b5b4b2d5fdf4","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shapes that enforce the requirement: boundary between bottom and lower regions is at point where shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.\n\nWe have ontology: property hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint linking ship to hullBoundaryPoint. Also quantity property shellInclinationAngle (object property) with range QuantityValue.\n\nWe need to represent that for each ship (owner target class), there is a hullBoundaryPoint via that property, and that point must have associated shellInclinationAngle value equal to 7 degrees.\n\nBut the ontology does not define the relationship between hullBoundaryPoint and shellInclinationAngle. Likely hullBoundaryPoint is a node that can have property shellInclinationAngle pointing to a QuantityValue with numericValue 7 and unit DEG.\n\nWe need to create SHACL shapes:\n\n- TargetClass: ship (or maybe the owner_class). The contract indicates target_owner null, but focus_set owner_class ship. So shape target: sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>.\n\n- Property shape for hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint: must have at least one value? Not specified but requirement defines boundary point. So maybe require exactly one, with value node of type hullBoundaryPoint.\n\n- Then for that hullBoundaryPoint node, need a property shape for shellInclinationAngle with numericValue 7 and unit DEG.\n\nWe need to use quantityEncoding: numeric_predicate qudt:numericValue and unit_predicate qudt:unit. So we need to enforce that the QuantityValue node has those.\n\nIn SHACL, we can use sh:property with sh:path <property>. For nested constraints, we can use sh:node to define a shape for the target node.\n\nThus define shape :ShipBoundaryShape: targetClass ship; property shape for hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint: sh:path ... ; sh:node :HullBoundaryShape.\n\nHullBoundaryShape: targetClass hullBoundaryPoint? Not necessary but the node shape can have sh:property shellInclinationAngle that points to a QuantityValue, and then enforce numeric value 7 and unit DEG.\n\nDefine shape for shellInclinationAngle property: sh:path <...#shellInclinationAngle> ; sh:node :AngleValueShape.\n\nAngleValueShape: targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ; sh:property numericValue with datatype xsd:decimal, sh:equals? There is no direct equals but we can set sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal . Also enforce unit property sh:property sh:path qudt:unit with sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG> .\n\nThus the SHACL graph.\n\nAlso include sh:declare for prefixes.\n\nAlso we must reflect unresolved aspects? The requirement text is present but we are correctly modeling.\n\nThe schema: property constraints.\n\nNo extra obligations.\n\nProvide SHACL with prefixes:\n\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\nDefine shapes with IRI maybe base: <https://example.org/shapes#ShipBoundaryShape> etc.\n\nWe'll use ex:.\n\nBut we can use blank nodes.\n\nBetter to assign IRIs:\n\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShipBoundaryShape> etc.\n\nWe must use exact canonical IRIs.\n\nWe'll use those.\n\nNow produce output:\n\n<BEGIN_SHACL>\n...turtle...\n<END_SHACL>\n\nMake sure to include sh:targetClass etc.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_80ccbd31fa1e9ca1","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that targets every ship and requires a hull‑boundary point\n# linked via the property hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint.\n# The linked hull‑boundary point must carry a shell inclination\n# angle of exactly 7 deg.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShipBoundaryShape>\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:node <https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#HullBoundaryShape> ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the hull‑boundary point referenced from a ship.\n# It must have a shellInclinationAngle property whose value is a\n# QUDT QuantityValue with numeric value 7 and unit degree.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#HullBoundaryShape>\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:hullBoundaryPoint ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shellInclinationAngle ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:node <https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShellAngleQuantityShape> ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the QUDT QuantityValue representing the shell inclination.\n# It must contain:\n#   - qudt:numericValue = 7 (decimal)\n#   - qudt:unit = unit:DEG\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShellAngleQuantityShape>\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:DEG ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":12979,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":12976,"cache_write_tokens":0,"input_tokens_per_turn":[12979],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[12976]},"output_tokens":1415,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":807,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1415],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":14394},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}